<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_WardenMother.xml   UtinniPatches - WARDEN_MOTHER_BEFRIENDING_1

  The Miasma's centrepiece giant, ruled by the owner 2026-09-23
  (miasma_fauna_roster_2026-09-23.md §6): "a not-so-gentle giant who can be
  befriended when its young call out for it and get stuck... able to lumber
  along in the water... but cannot get on dry land." Franchise-free per Q11a
  and SEA_BEASTS_TIER_RULING_1 — she is invented, not canon, so RM_ (the
  earlier RUT_WardenMother name in RM_CompTerritorialAnchor.cs's own header
  comment was always wrong for this reason, per that file's own retraction).

  Spawned exclusively via RUT_GenStep_CrecheScatterer
  (Defs/MapGeneration/RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer.xml, RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces),
  never via <wildAnimals> — zero biome wild-spawn commonality, matching the
  already-shipped GenStep's own "the GenStep is their only entry" posture.
  That GenStep's own validator (RM_ScattererValidator_BrineShallowWater)
  places her crèche site on brine-side shallow water, and
  RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn's SetAnchor() call anchors her to the
  RUT_CrecheMarker placed at that same site — "her crèche is in the
  shallows" is therefore true by construction, not by a separate mechanism.

  bodySize 8: bigger than the evicted AA_OvergrownColossus (6, cast_assignment.csv)
  per "the giant lane here is owned by warden mothers... a random giant
  dilutes them" (item's own Watch-out), smaller than the whale-scale
  RM_Reefback (32, TerminalBiomes/RM_SeaBeasts_Invented.xml) since she is an
  amphibious melee predator, not a leviathan drifting the open sea.
  INVENTED-BUILD figure, no size named by the roster beyond "enormous."

  waterSeeker + waterCellCost 1: real vanilla RaceProperties fields
  (Verse/RaceProperties.cs, used identically by every Odyssey coastal/sea
  creature and this repo's own RM_Reefback) that bias the normal pathfinder
  toward water for this race — a genuine, low-risk, zero-new-code nudge
  layered under the three water-only pieces in RM_CompWaterLocked.cs's own
  header (wander validator / target validator / tick backstop). It does NOT
  by itself make land impassable; MEASURED against the decompiled engine
  before writing this (Source/Verse/AI/Pawn_PathFollower.cs:739,
  Source/Verse/PathFinderCostTuning.cs:47) — it only ever discounts the cost
  of a water cell, never inflates a land cell's.

  Wildness 1.0 (same convention as every SEA_BEASTS_TIER_RULING_1 creature,
  RM_Reefback included): "she is never tamed" per the roster's own repeated
  ⛔. disableMating true, predator/canBePredatorPrey false: she is a set-piece
  defender anchored to one site, not part of the map's ordinary food web —
  same posture as RM_Reefback's own reasoning, reused rather than re-derived.

  lifeExpectancy 45 (INVENTED-BUILD; the roster's §6a rules "she dies of age,
  foreshadowed hard from the first day" but names no figure) is deliberately
  short for a creature this size, so a colony that raises her stranded young
  across a normal campaign has a real chance of outliving her — the
  succession payoff (§6a) depends on that. Full succession-on-death (the
  young inheriting the crèche) and the art/UX foreshadowing (slowing
  measurably, an NPC who tells you) are NOT built here — filed as
  WARDEN_MOTHER_SUCCESSION_1.

  CompProperties_TerritorialAnchor dutyDef RM_AnchorGuard / anchorRadius 16:
  her reach. CompProperties_WaterLocked: the movement constraint's own tick
  backstop (RM_CompWaterLocked.cs). Both MayRequire
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards, matching this file's own hard
  About.xml dependency on that mod.

  No art: texPath below does not resolve to anything yet (checked
  infrastructure/artpipe/done/, _artsrc/, registry.jsonl and
  art_status.json by subject first, per the owner's 2026-09-20 standing
  rule — nothing found for "warden mother" under any spelling). A
  fill_queue.py job is owed and not queued by this pass (the daemon does
  not run on the Mac); same "advisory texPath warning, expected pre-art"
  posture MIASMA_FLORA_ROSTER_1/MIASMA_FAUNA_FLOOR_ROSTER_1 already shipped
  under.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_WardenMother</defName>
    <label>warden mother</label>
    <description>Barnacled, scarred, and older than anything else that swims these shallows — you can see it in how slowly she moves now. She goes wherever the water goes, and nowhere else; the few metres of dry ground between her and anything on land might as well be another world. Lethal to anything she can reach. Not tame, not tameable, and not gentle — but she remembers who freed her young from a drying pool, and she will not touch you for it.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.6</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>0</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-20</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>55</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.55</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.65</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <Wildness>1.0</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>crushing bite</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.0</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>flipper slam</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>18</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.6</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>Pinniped</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <canBePredatorPrey>false</canBePredatorPrey>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <disableMating>true</disableMating>
      <baseBodySize>8</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>7</baseHealthScale>
      <foodType>OmnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <waterSeeker>true</waterSeeker>
      <waterCellCost>1</waterCellCost>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>45</lifeExpectancy>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.15</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.4</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
    <comps>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_TerritorialAnchor">
        <dutyDef>RM_AnchorGuard</dutyDef>
        <anchorRadius>16</anchorRadius>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_WaterLocked">
        <checkIntervalTicks>60</checkIntervalTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_WardenMother</defName>
    <label>warden mother</label>
    <race>RM_WardenMother</race>
    <combatPower>1400</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0</ecoSystemWeight>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <moveSpeedFactorByTerrainTag>
      <li>
        <key>Water</key>
        <value>1.8</value>
      </li>
    </moveSpeedFactorByTerrainTag>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Miasma/WardenMother/WardenMother</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>3.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Miasma/WardenMother/WardenMother</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>5.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Miasma/WardenMother/WardenMother</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>7.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
